WEBVTT

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.160
<i>Say goodbye hello</i>

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.370
<i>Kurikaesu kimi to boku</i>
<i>megurimeguru towa ni</i>

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:05.880
<i>Bokura no yukue</i> wa...

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:12.380
<i>Soba ni iru to mienaku naru mono wa nani?</i>

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:20.060
<i>Irotoridori no ai to yasashisa</i>

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:26.760
<i>Sasai na koto de kizutsukiatta hibi kara</i>

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:33.070
<i>Wasureteta mono omoidashita yo</i>

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:40.380
<i>Bokura no ashioto wa</i>
<i>mirai e tsuzuku "kiseki"</i>

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:48.050
<i>Utsuriyuku keshiki no naka</i> de... <i>itsudemo</i>

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.090
<i>Say goodbye hello</i>

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:55.160
<i>Kurikaesu kimi to boku</i>
<i>megurimeguru towa ni</i>

00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:02.230
<i>Mirai wo egakidasu kono</i>
<i>merodi sekai kawaru made</i>

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.230
<i>Say goodbye hello</i>

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:09.470
<i>Itsu datte hi wa mata</i>
<i>nobori kurikaesu towa ni</i>

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:20.320
<i>Bokura no yukue wo terashidasu yo</i>

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.190
Nataru?

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.660
Nataru!

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.670
It's been a long time, Birdy.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.170
Nataru!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.140
Ow!

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.870
Oh, sorry!

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.140
Don't forget how absurdly strong you are!

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.970
Sorry!

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.880
You haven't changed a bit, Birdy.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.180
Are you sure?

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.680
Yep. You're just the same
as when we were kids.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.180
No, no. I'm taller, for one thing.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.350
Plus, I'm stronger than I used to be.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.550
Sheesh...

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.890
Hey, who is this guy?

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.460
Huh?

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.390
"Shinmyou"?

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.830
Yeah. "Nataru Shinmyou."

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.300
At this point, my Earth name suits me best.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.140
Huh, so it's the same
as my "Shion Arita" name?

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.910
"Shion," huh? That's cute.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.140
But when did you get here, Nataru?

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:25.480
That's right... I guess I didn't even
get the chance to say goodbye to you.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.850
It's been fourteen years
already since I got here, I think.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.320
This place is nice.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:34.260
The air's polluted and
there are too many people.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.890
They're always having some war somewhere.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:39.900
The civilization on this
planet is pretty half-baked.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.900
But nobody discriminates
against you just for being Altan.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:49.270
You must remember how the
Altans were discriminated against

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.710
and persecuted after the
Central Tower terrorism.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.590
I just barely managed to escape with my dad

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.560
before we were put in an isolation camp.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.960
And, we eventually made our way here.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.630
Ah, sorry, that turned gloomy.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.100
So, what are you up to, Birdy?

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.140
I became a Federation investigator.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.470
Investigator? Huh, good for you.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.370
Yep.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.440
So, are you on a case?

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.910
Sorry, I can't give you confidential info.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.620
Wow, you've really grown up, Birdy.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.550
To think you're the same girl
who once peed her pants and cried...

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:40.390
Jeez, you still remember that?!

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.300
Was that guy a childhood friend?

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:54.570
Yep. He sure surprised me!

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.560
So like me and Hayamiya, huh?

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.780
Take that!

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.110
You must've picked on Nataru, too.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.650
Why would you say that?! I was a good girl.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:08.280
I'm so sure you weren't.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.790
Hey, now.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:12.760
Say, what's the "Central Tower terrorism"?

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:15.690
I don't want to tell you. It dramatized me.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:19.100
Birdy, it's called "traumatized."

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.500
Oh, crap! I have to go to school!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:26.940
Someone murdered Rianshel
before I could detain him.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:31.110
I can't imagine an Earthling is
capable of murdering a Gienkan.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.010
Did they have a falling-out?

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.510
That seems likely.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:37.950
Which makes it all the more crucial
that we arrest the remaining escapees.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.820
Hurry.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:43.550
I've obtained a clue. It's a mimesis chip.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:44.820
I see.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.960
It's equipped with a function
that eradicates the corpse

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:52.130
should the user's vital
functions cease, destroying evidence.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:55.870
It must be a cutting-edge Granadan chip.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.730
That's not something that would hit
the market all the way out in the boonies.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.360
We'll look into this on our end too.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.250
You sure it's okay not to tell him
about that Nataru guy being here?

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.680
It's fine. He's not a criminal.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.990
Plus, it's not like Altan refugees
on Earth are all that unusual.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:18.820
I want to leave him in peace.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:30.870
"Who the hell said there were aliens here?"

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.370
Seriously! Who's stirring up
these poor junior high kids?!

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:34.870
"It was in the godly Muroto's book."
Seriously! Who's stirring up
these poor junior high kids?!

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.770
"It was in the godly Muroto's book."

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.070
It's me?!

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.180
What is this?

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:46.920
Check it out! It's the "I
saw an alien" thread fest!

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.690
Whoa, there's lots of UFO vids.

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.420
Do you believe in UFOs, Chigira?

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:55.460
Not really... you know?

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.560
Nobody believes in aliens these days.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.260
Hey, this looks interesting!

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.030
"Sketch of 'Mysterious Disappearance at
the First-Class Hotel' Suspect Released"

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.700
A sketch of the woman thought to be involved

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:05.270
in the mysterious disappearance at
the first-class hotel has been released!

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:06.800
Gah!

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.240
Not good!

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.800
Come on, let's check it out!

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.880
What the hell is this?!

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:18.310
This is worse than some
kindergartener's drawing.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.380
In a way, it might be genius.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:22.620
Really, boys are so dumb.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.250
What?! Don't lump me in with these guys!

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.090
Thank goodness!

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:35.060
Hey Capella! I'll take a coffee.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.800
A-A coffee?

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.270
Yep. Thanks.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.900
R-Right!

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:47.910
It's all your fault... It's all your fault!

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.350
It's a mimesis chip.

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:53.650
If you know something about it, tell me.

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:56.920
All Shion Arita's plans for
next month are still provisional...

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:59.320
"Shion Arita's Schedule"

00:07:59.320 --> 00:07:59.790
All Shion Arita's plans for
next month are still provisional...

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.530
Okay, fine, I'll work.

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:03.960
Well?

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:08.100
This is just a rumor, all right?

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:13.870
Our Altan network has been around for ages.

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:15.470
It was formed by connections

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:18.340
between people who fled to
Earth for their lives long ago.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.480
But lately people say

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:24.680
that there are "escape men" among
the Altans who left the Federation.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.980
"Escape men"?

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:30.850
They'd probably be able
to smuggle in mimesis chips.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:33.620
Where can I find these escape men?

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.460
Why don't you do a little
of the investigating yourself?

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.130
Shinmyou!

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:43.670
Oh, Dr. Shimano.

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:46.340
How are you feeling?
Are you taking your meds?

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:47.300
Yes.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.240
If you need anything, just let me know.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.670
Thank you.

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:55.310
By the way, is that your girlfriend?

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.880
You want to know how I came to Earth?

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:03.490
Yeah. I have my reasons...

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:04.920
Investigative ones?

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.820
Yeah...

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:11.830
But I was still just a kid back then, you know.

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:15.100
I just ran like Dad told me to.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.200
Then could I ask your dad?

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:22.270
Sorry, but some things happened,
and we don't have much contact.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:25.240
I don't even know whether
he's alive or dead right now.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:26.670
Oh...

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.210
Hey...

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.610
Nataru!

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.510
Shoko.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:42.690
Shion Arita.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:44.520
So you know her.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.700
Hello there, Ma'am!

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.530
Why are you with that stupid pinup girl?

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:57.110
Well, we're childhood friends.
We just happened to bump into each other.

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.300
Childhood friends?

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.950
Nataru... do you
remember what day tomorrow is?

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.080
Tomorrow?

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.820
Yeah, I remember.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:14.090
Okay, see you later, Bir... er, Miss Arita.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.420
I'll be in touch.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.260
Okay.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.770
Hey, Tsutomu.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.940
What?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:31.840
Do you think I said
something to upset that girl?

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:33.670
You mean Shoko?

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:38.480
She seemed kind of angry...

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:39.820
That was definitely jealousy.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.120
Huh?

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.790
Because you seemed to be
getting on so well with Nataru.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.660
Jealous because of <i>that?</i>

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.190
Don't you get it?

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.430
Get what?

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:51.090
Her young girl's heart.

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:52.700
Young girl's heart?

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:54.960
Shoko likes Nataru.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.030
Really?

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:57.970
She's in love...

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.870
Why are you talking like
<i>you</i> know so much about it?

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:01.640
You've never been in love, Birdy?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.340
I don't have time to let my
hormones run wild like you!

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:04.670
I knew it...

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:08.810
Sheesh! I've had enough of you
Earthlings and your hormonal urges!

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:09.880
I know, I'll take a bath.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:10.870
Hey, now!

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:23.290
Ah, today's your brother's
monthly death anniversary, isn't it?

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.690
Yes.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.820
"Kagami Family"

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:34.360
Don't worry about me,
big brother. I'm doing fine.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.870
Nataru.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:46.350
Dad?

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.020
Hello.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:51.250
Yeah. Okay.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:53.390
Well, shall we go?

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:55.390
Did something happen to your dad?

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.380
He just told me to visit
him since it's been a while.

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:11.410
Please take this.
I'm afraid it's all I can do for you.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.680
I feel bad, letting you do this all the time.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:20.080
Nonsense. My family owes you a debt
that cannot be repaid for generations.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:23.420
Really, that was a full thousand
years ago; you have no obligation now.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:25.250
A thousand years is nothing.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:34.630
Oh, welcome.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:38.200
I was just visiting. I'll be going now.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:40.190
Okay, goodbye then.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:47.480
So that lady was here again?

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:50.610
She's not "that lady"; she's "Ms. Irma."

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:52.280
Okay, "Ms. Irma" it is.

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:52.450
"Shinmyou Books"
Okay, "Ms. Irma" it is.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.480
"Shinmyou Books"

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:06.490
I'm coming in.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:09.660
Huh?

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:15.670
Bonsai, Dad? You're all about the
stereotypical old man hobbies now.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:20.010
The day will come when
you'll see the appeal, too.

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:22.950
Can't say I particularly <i>want</i> to see it...

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:25.570
So, what did you want to discuss?

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:30.790
Nataru, have you come here
recently while I wasn't in?

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:33.290
Nope, I haven't.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.990
So it wasn't you.

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:37.260
What are you talking about?

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:39.090
Rianshel.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:40.500
Who's that?

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.330
He was killed.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.460
Huh, sounds scary.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.260
Don't use the power.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:57.450
That power will destroy you,
do you understand?

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:58.210
That's why...

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:00.050
I know.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:04.890
You're really getting old, Dad. I'm fine.

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:07.720
I wouldn't use something like that.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.870
Dammit, that old hag is a slave driver.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.740
Who's an "old hag"?

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:26.210
Now, just who was it who came crying
to me begging to let her stay here?

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:30.250
I owe every day of my life to you, Ms. Irma.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:32.480
As long as you understand that.

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:35.510
Welco...

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:37.980
Hi, Capella!

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:41.720
Here you are.

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:47.200
This is special coffee, Miss Birdy.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.570
Thanks.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:50.930
This is pathetic.

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:55.170
Why should I, the one they
called the Grim Reaper, have to...

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:57.710
...make coffee for that idiot?

00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:00.540
I heard an interesting rumor, Birdy.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.450
Really? That's my Irma. Tell me!

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:08.250
Well, I will if you do
another job as Shion Arita.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.890
Aw, I knew it...

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:13.620
Okay, I'll count on you for
this animal-costume show.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:17.960
Someone saw a man who
smells like a Garbelantan.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.730
Where? Where was he?

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:23.100
Around the other side of Aoyama.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.730
Thanks!

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:28.400
Capella, come clean up!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.800
All right!

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:35.710
What a waste... You drink it.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:36.580
Huh?

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.210
Who else?

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:44.990
Hey, Birdy!

00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:47.660
Hold on a second.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:50.330
They're right... it smells like a Garbelantan.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.160
An alien?

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:52.830
Yeah. Tuto!

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:55.460
Verify the Garbelantan, please.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:00.000
Agrazume?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.340
A criminal?

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:02.960
An escapee.

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.660
The target's approaching?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.600
That way?

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.150
Jeez, these are in the way!

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:15.580
Birdy!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:22.420
Hey, Birdy, this is dangerous!
If someone sees us...

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:42.540
Agrazume, right?
You're under arrest for jail breaking.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:44.880
Whatever do you mean, young lady?

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:47.870
Are you sure you haven't got the wrong man?

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.960
Why, that...

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:06.870
Boss, the car's finally been delivered.

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:09.300
It's used, but it's shiny as new!

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.870
Yeah, it's my shiny old car!

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:13.700
Step right in, Boss.

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:18.900
Why me?!

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.650
He's trying to escape into the Roppongi ruins!

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:27.050
I know.

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:39.730
Got you!

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.110
Ow!

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:46.270
Are you okay, Birdy?

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:49.410
I guess this is tough without my protector...

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:50.380
What now?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.450
Tuto's sensor won't do any good here.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:54.520
It won't?

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:56.550
Damn it...

00:17:56.550 --> 00:18:01.520
That's right, they did say there
was an investigator on this planet...

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.510
Agrazume, I presume?

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:10.100
Who are you?!

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:13.400
You're the one who
killed Rianshel, aren't you!

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.100
He was punished for his crimes.

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:17.710
Are you a damn Altan?!

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:19.110
That's right.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:23.080
A mere Altan, challenging <i>me?</i>

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:28.650
I'm not like Rianshel. I'll kill
you off with my own hands.

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:31.280
Well, you've piqued my interest.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.460
I won't give you an easy death.

00:18:52.010 --> 00:18:56.480
How does it feel to have
your arm torn off by an Altan?

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:57.910
You bastard!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:02.120
You figured that it'd be fine
to experiment with the Ryunka

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:06.760
on a planet where the people
looked like Altans, right?

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:09.690
That it wouldn't matter if all the natives died.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:13.360
Because who cares when the victims
are practically Altans anyway?

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:14.790
St-Stop!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.470
What's taking Shoko so long?

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.810
No point worrying about it, Kagami.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.610
The movie will start without us!

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:30.150
We can just catch the next showing.

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:31.980
There's no need to hurry.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:35.480
Well, true, but... Oh, a text message.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:37.320
Sheesh, it's Shoko?

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.900
What was that?!

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:49.130
An earthquake?

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.120
Kagami, was that...

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:55.560
Kagami?

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:01.870
Kagami.

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:19.720
What the hell?

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:21.890
Kagami!

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:24.760
Kagami!

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:33.880
Please let me go... Let me go!

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:35.070
No.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.880
Suffer all you can, and then die!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.710
Spare me!

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:37.500
Five more.

00:23:11.270 --> 00:23:14.840
<i>Hi, this is Birdy Cephon Altira, yessiree!</i>

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:17.770
<i>Whoops, no, this is Birdy!</i>

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:20.680
<i>The people who lost their homes</i>

00:23:20.680 --> 00:23:24.250
<i>are living in tents in a refugee</i>
<i>camp near the Roppongi ruins.</i>

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:25.850
<i>It seems really rough!</i>

00:23:25.850 --> 00:23:28.350
<i>While Tsutomu and the others</i>
<i>do interviews at the camp,</i>

00:23:28.350 --> 00:23:31.220
<i>they meet an energetic</i>
<i>little girl named Marina</i>

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:35.090
<i>and get mixed up in something awful!</i>

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:39.080
<i>Violin, is that girl really so much like me?</i>
